{
  "key": "E011",
  "title": "Lag-aware joint control under cooling degradation, heat and slow coolant loops",
  "research_question": "Does planning with the coolant loop's lag (joint_lag) remove the overheating that steady-state joint control showed under a slow loop in E010, and at what energy and service cost?",
  "hypothesis": "Conditions: 3 cold-plate states x 3 ambient temperatures (20/30/40 C) x 3 plants (quasi-steady; 40 kg loop, 1 K/min ramp; 150 kg loop, 0.25 K/min ramp), S6 load profile, measured leakage slope and clock sensitivity. H1: joint_lag records zero chip-seconds throttled in all 27 conditions. H2: joint_lag records zero chip-seconds above 80 C in all 18 dynamic-loop conditions. H3: with the quasi-steady plant, joint_lag's results equal joint's in all 9 conditions (identical decisions). H4: joint_lag uses no more energy per successful task than joint in every condition (95% CI upper bound of joint_lag/joint - 1 below +0.5%) and less than independent (CI upper bound below 0) wherever independent exceeded 80 C. H5: joint_lag's SLO violations (seed mean) exceed the larger of joint's and independent's by at most 2 per run in every condition.",
  "null_hypothesis": "Modelling the loop's lag does not change safety or energy relative to steady-state joint control.",
  "independent_variables": [
    "cold-plate state (3)",
    "ambient (3)",
    "plant (3)",
    "policy (independent, joint, joint_lag)"
  ],
  "dependent_variables": [
    "chip_s_over_target",
    "chip_s_throttled",
    "peak_T_j_C",
    "slo_violations",
    "success_rate",
    "E_per_success_kJ"
  ],
  "controlled_variables": [
    "S6 load profile",
    "seeds 0-4",
    "warm start",
    "leakage matched to the measured slope (kappa 0.02)",
    "clock sensitivity from M001",
    "twin knows the true cold-plate state and the loop's mass and ramp limit"
  ],
  "baseline": "joint and independent within each condition",
  "configuration": "Every cell: {'beta_compute': 0.983, 'beta_memory': 0.0, 'kappa_leak': 0.02, 'p_leak_ref': 28.962}. Plants: {'quasi': {'loop_mass_kg': 0.0, 'tsup_ramp_K_per_min': 0.0}, 'dyn40': {'loop_mass_kg': 40.0, 'tsup_ramp_K_per_min': 1.0}, 'dyn150': {'loop_mass_kg': 150.0, 'tsup_ramp_K_per_min': 0.25}}. Cold-plate states: {'clean': {'r_cond': 0.035, 'r_conv_ref': 0.015}, 'moderate': {'r_cond': 0.04, 'r_conv_ref': 0.0225}, 'severe': {'r_cond': 0.045, 'r_conv_ref': 0.03}}.",
  "evaluation_criteria": "Thermal outcomes and SLO violations as seed means over 5 seeds; energy as paired relative differences with 95% t-CI.",
  "known_limitations": "The controller knows the loop's mass and ramp limit exactly; the loop model is a single well-mixed tank. Leakage matched at one operating point from one consumer card; voltage-frequency form is the registry placeholder. 5 seeds. independent and joint cells repeat E010's design (40 kg) and add the 150 kg loop.",
  "disclosure": "Before registration, one exploratory run (severe fouling, 40 C ambient, S6 profile shortened to 1 h, seed 0, 40 kg loop and quasi-steady plant) compared joint_lag with joint and independent: with the 40 kg loop joint spent 617 chip-s above 80 C (26 throttled), independent 404 (94), joint_lag 0, and joint_lag used 8.50 vs 8.64 kJ per successful task; with the quasi-steady plant joint_lag matched joint exactly. That run is kept as a regression test. E010's results were known. The 150 kg plant was not tried before registration.",
